# Review: decisions/invariants-and-provisionals.md (turn 13)

## Overall assessment

This file is acceptable as-is. It delivers a complete decision record — 30 invariants with derivations or paid-for counterexamples, 16 provisional decisions with reasons and flip conditions, 4 explicit handoff amendments with evidence and downstream consequences, plus boundary ownership, source-conflict resolutions, and evidence debt — all with full epistemic tagging. Spot-checks against the handoff, blueprints, candidate sources, and all six accepted contracts confirm the extraction claims, rule-ID citations, and amendment evidence. The two concerns below are cosmetic citation-precision notes that do not affect acceptance or downstream use.

## Protocol, completeness, structure

- **Protocol.** The raw deliverable (`runs/turn8-20/deliverables/turn13.md`) opens with ````markdown:decisions/invariants-and-provisionals.md`, closes with ```` ``` ```` followed by `<!-- TURN_END:13 -->`, and has no content outside the fence except the marker. Manifest item 13 is `decisions/invariants-and-provisionals.md`. The tree file is byte-identical to the fenced inner content (verified by diff). Compliant.
- **Completeness.** The file ends at a coherent boundary (§10 change control, final bullet on shipping discipline). Not truncated.
- **Structure.** Matches what the design conversation and developer prompt require of this item: invariant/provisional distinction with reasoning preserved, a "handoff amendments" section recording every amendment with specific evidence and downstream consequence, and synthesis (conflict resolution, boundary lines) rather than concatenation.

## Verification performed

- **Epistemic coverage.** Programmatic scan: every substantive paragraph and table row carries one of `[extracted:/[inferred:/[proposed:/[uncertain:` (140 tagged claims, 0 untagged substantive lines).
- **Extraction spot-checks (all confirmed in cited sources):** the eight playbook names (`capability_profile.txt` §2); the six evaluation dimensions (`job_search_queries.txt` §4: `can_do_70_percent`, `hard_blockers`, `playbooks_matched`, `would_tolerate`, `pay_ok`, `legibility_gap`); the six null reasons and the capability/opportunity/result enums verbatim (handoff Part VI); the nine connector verbs in both the handoff (Part VI) and Hellscape §§5.2–5.3; the five attempt axes with authorities (handoff Part VI); the seven semantic boundaries and `circus-tent-cf`/`circus-tent-bo` aliases (handoff Part V); "top five this week" and the "produce a real application earlier" invitation (handoff Parts VII, IX); `/run status=completed` → execution completion, fixture-authority sealing, the invalid isolation control, and the `_elapsed()` defect (Hellscape §§1.3, 4.5, 5.5, 13); all four `INCOMPLETE` markers verbatim and all nine `ASSUMED` values (crawler §§0, 15–16); the ten-slot all-`HttpClient` pagination matrix, IL dormant Phase B slot, and zero Page pool (crawler §§3.1, 10.3, 13.A); `browser_oxide` inventory and `browser_oxide::Page` thread confinement with zero Camoufox mentions (crawler §§0, 9); the self-referral/contact-reveal prohibition (crawler §§13.B, 13.D); the m0 physical-operator final-submission rule (qualification doc, Setup and execution); Hellscape's broader result enum including `blocked`/`not_applicable` and manual-session `not_exercised` (§4.4); `fabricationLog`, `shared/firestore-contracts`, `$X+`, zone rules, and bachelor's-required flag-not-exclude (get-a-job sources); single-binary deployment, SQLite/WAL, and M1-disabled fingerprint capture (Hellscape §§3.1, 11.3, 14).
- **Cross-file consistency.** All cited rule IDs exist in the accepted contracts: `EK-JOURNAL`, `EK-PROVENANCE`, `EK-NULL`, `EK-MANUAL`, `EK-REPLAY`, `EK-LEASE`, `EK-LEASE-RESTART`; `LIFE-ORIGIN`, `LIFE-RECONCILE`, `LIFE-LATE-EVIDENCE`, `LIFE-TIME`, `LIFE-LINEAGE`, `LIFE-MANUAL`; `EXT-PREPARE`, `EXT-START`, `EXT-IDEMPOTENCY`; `kernel-jcs-sha256/1`; `owner-domain-extents/1` under `x-proposed-mechanisms`; `derived_from` same-kind lineage; job/attempt/session domain layouts (`crawler`/`downstream`, five axes, `application`/`observation`/`diagnostic`). All six contracts are `0.1.0`; six companion conformance documents exist; the binding document holds separate BrowserOxide and Camoufox schemas with separate suite instances. The packaging non-selection (§6.1) matches contract 03's open-packaging rule.
- **Amendment discipline.** HA-01 through HA-04 each name the handoff statement, give specific source evidence, state a replacement conclusion, and name downstream consequences. No silent overrides found. Notably, HA-02's narrowing of the shared-core claim and HA-03's day-one lane both execute flip conditions the handoff itself invites ("if the shared surface turns out to be small, then the cut is wrong"; "if you see a way to produce a real application earlier, take it"), and HA-04's "five suites" conflict is real (handoff Part VIII enumerates six suite-bearing contracts, then says "five").
- **Failure-mode review.** No fabricated citations, no invented enumerations (all counts and enums verified), no collapsed distinctions (claim/fact, five axes, capability/opportunity/result, framework healing vs. registry learning are all preserved), no silent re-litigation, no restatement-as-synthesis.

## Concerns

- **Title-contrast gloss cites only the playbook source** — §1, line 14 ("eight reusable playbooks—not a preferred list of job titles," cited `[extracted: 6-get-a-job.xml.txt, capability_profile.txt §2]`). The eight playbook names are in §2 as cited, but the "not titles" rationale lives in `job_search_queries.txt` ("title filters are the wrong primary key"). The claim is true and sourced elsewhere in the file's own §8/P-16 reasoning; the citation is merely incomplete. Severity: cosmetic.
- **`extracted` slightly overstates a backlog-scope claim** — §8.1, line 203 ("not four prerequisites for manual applications or an Illinois-only feed," tagged `[extracted: 1-handoff-brief.txt Parts I and VII]`). The handoff establishes backlog-not-milestone; the extension to manual applications follows from HA-03 reasoning and would be more precisely tagged `[inferred]`. Severity: cosmetic.

## Recommendation

**Accept with notes.** The file meets the manifest item's requirements: complete, protocol-compliant, epistemically disciplined, cross-consistent with all six contracts, and careful in its amendment discipline. The two cosmetic notes above may be folded into any future revision but need no action before downstream turns (prd/00–05) proceed.
